What this means in plain language: you may use, study, change, and share
this software. If you run a modified version of it as a network service,
you must make the modified source code available to the service's users
under the same license. That network-use clause is deliberate: it keeps
this public-good infrastructure from being captured by any single
operator, including one who never distributes a copy.
